{
 "_comment": "Namespaces whose metrics follow Datadog's AWS integration (scripts/import-cloud-metrics.mjs merges them into server/seeds/integrations/cloud/aws-metrics.json): `statistic` is the one Datadog publishes under the metric's bare name (the crawler names the others .sum / .maximum), `unit` Datadog's unit, `datadog_name` where Datadog's name isn't the snake-cased CloudWatch name, `variant` the name segment Datadog adds for a dimension set (aws.ecs.cluster.*, aws.ecs.service.*, ecs.containerinsights.family.*), `group` the dimension a chart splits by and `filter` a tag every query keeps (WAF publishes each web ACL's totals as rule:ALL). Names, statistics, dimensions and units are facts from the AWS documentation pages in `doc`. `overrides` patch the other namespaces' metrics where Datadog's AWS integration differs from aws-cdk-lib (its metric lists on docs.datadoghq.com: counts published as their Sum, gauges as their Average), list a latency's `percentiles` (CloudWatch's extended statistics, published as .p95 etc.), daily metrics' `period` (86400: S3's storage metrics and Storage Lens, read once a day for the previous day) and metrics the sources lack (S3's request metrics, per bucket filter).",
